= Introduction

== Context

This document aims to establish a meta model to writing documentation in the field of computer science. It tries to establish thinking patterns, workflows, concepts and tools that guides software craftsman to write and maintain documentations that are consistent, accurate and easy to understand.

In the end, there's one core idea this document tries to achieve, that being:

Writing documentation for software should so trivially easy that there is never an excuse to not do it.

== About

=== How does this meta model differe from other models?

There are many other great models and templates for writing software documentations, like arc42, ... and similar. Some of these models are even featured within this meta model when talking about the how-to's. This document, however, tries to establish both a thinking pattern when writing any sort of documentation about a software product, as well as workflows and tools that help when actually writing documentation.

Think of this document like a guided tour through a art museum. In a art museum, you might walk through diffrent historic eras of art, hearing about the era itself before taking a closer look at some specific pieces. Similary, this document will walk you through diffrent types of documentations, talking about each type in general before taking a closere look at some specific examples.

